{"content":[{"c":["MATTITHIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Levite and Shallum’s firstborn son, who was in charge of making the baked cakes that accompanied the offerings in the temple (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.31","r":"1Chr.9.31","rawR":"1Chr.9.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.31","value":"1Chr.9.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:31"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Musician appointed by the Levites to play the lyre, along with five others, when the ark was brought to Jerusalem in David’s time (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.18,21","r":"1Chr.15.18,21","rawR":"1Chr.15.18,21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.18,21","value":"1Chr.15.18,21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:18, 21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.5","r":"1Chr.16.5","rawR":"1Chr.16.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.5","value":"1Chr.16.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. One of Jeduthun’s six sons, who was a musician in David’s time (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.3,21","r":"1Chr.25.3,21","rawR":"1Chr.25.3,21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.3,21","value":"1Chr.25.3,21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 25:3, 21"},"); perhaps identifiable with #2 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Nebo’s son, who divorced his foreign wife as commanded by Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.43","r":"Ezra.10.43","rawR":"Ezra.10.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.43","value":"Ezra.10.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:43"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. One who stood to Ezra’s right when Ezra read the law to the people after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.8.4","r":"Neh.8.4","rawR":"Neh.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.8.4","value":"Neh.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 8:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mattithiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":